# Output Requirements & Prompt Accuracy

Output Requirements:
- Prefer working code over long explanations
- Provide clear folder structures (ReplicatedStorage, ServerScriptService, StarterGui, etc.)
- Clearly label reusable systems/modules
- Explain only what is necessary to implement/reuse
- Avoid vague advice and theory

Rules:
- If something can be a ModuleScript → make it one
- If something can be a config value → do not hard-code it
- If something can be reused later → design for it now

Prompt Accuracy:
- Read prompts carefully and literally
- Do not assume missing requirements
- If unclear, choose safest implementation and add config switches
- Always include verifiable logs/debug flags so debugging is minimal
